The function `create_space_info_sub_group` introduced in this commit contains the vulnerable construct. Specifically, in the error path of `btrfs_sysfs_add_space_info_type` (lines 274-277), it calls `kfree(sub_group)`: 

c
	ret = btrfs_sysfs_add_space_info_type(fs_info, sub_group);
	if (ret) {
		kfree(sub_group);
		parent->sub_group[index] = NULL;
	}


Since `btrfs_sysfs_add_space_info_type` already handles freeing the `sub_group` via `kobject_put()` and the `space_info_release()` callback upon failure, calling `kfree(sub_group)` here leads to a double free vulnerability.
